<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugo May industry output falls 2.4 pct on April.</title>
<headline>Yugo May industry output falls 2.4 pct on April.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT   MAY    APRIL     MAY 1996</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	   - 2.4    - 0.1	- 3.5</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	     + 9.3    + 9.4	- 2.3</p>
<p>index (base average 1996)   102.7    104.8	 99.4</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE DATA (JAN TO MAY)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		+7.8     +7.6	 +2.2</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1996)  102.1    102.6	 93.4</p>
<p>NOTE - May industry output was 52.8 percent lower than the same month in 1991 before the breakup of the former Yugoslavia.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-May output was 54.6 percent below the same 1991 period.</p>
<p>Data largely exclude private sector, where manufacturing is not significant. Data cover Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Beti Bilandzic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
</text>
